How to Regenerate the Database and Raw Exports

The database and raw data files are generated using the generate_data.py script. The script creates a new SQLite database called bigbasket_capstone.db and generates the raw CSV files orders_raw.csv and products.csv.
To regenerate the files, open a terminal in the project folder and run:
python generate_data.py
The script will recreate the database and generate the following files:
bigbasket_capstone.db – SQLite database containing the project tables and data.
orders_raw.csv – Raw order data used for the Python/Pandas analysis. The data intentionally contains some missing values, duplicate rows, inconsistent text formatting, and outliers for the data-cleaning tasks.
products.csv – Product information including product name, category, supplier, and unit price.
The complete data-generation process can be found in generate_data.py.

SQL Analysis

The SQL tasks are divided into three files:

01_foundations.sql – Contains the foundation SQL tasks, including basic queries and table-level analysis.
02_aggregation_joins.sql – Contains aggregation and JOIN-based analysis.
03_reporting.sql – Contains reporting and business-focused SQL queries.
verify.sql – Contains queries used to verify the database and results.

